# Scacelith - Eesti
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals: one|other ("1 käik|5 käiku").
# Register: formal "te" (lowercase) in sentences; buttons, menu entries and short commands use the bare
# imperative ("Salvesta", "Anna alla") or a noun. Chess terms follow the Estonian glossary (lipp, vanker,
# oda, ratsu, ettur; tuli, matt, patt, viik; piece letters K L V O R). Titles in capitals.
# A placeholder never takes a case ending: a clock time ("4:59") follows "pärast" ("{0} pärast"), a
# duration in words ("5 minutit") follows "oodake" ("Oodake {0}"), a player's name follows "mängija"
# ("mängija {0} kellal"), a server's name follows "serveris / serverisse" ("serverisse {0}").
# Keep the sections: other parts of the game add their keys in sections of their own.

